# Neo Learn Additive parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.2). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnAdditive
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnAdd
class NeoLearnAdditiveMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching additive synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. Up to 64 sine partials of a harmonic series with a brightness tilt, odd/even balance, a partial count, inharmonicity (stiff-string stretching), a comb of notches across the partials and a slow per-partial shimmer, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for organs, pads, bells, choirs and pure tones, or to learn how additive synthesis works.

group Core
SpectralTilt     "Brightness Tilt" 0 1000 800 lin -24 6 dB/oct 1
    id spectral_tilt
    how Adjusts the amplitude roll-off slope across all active upper sine partials relative to the fundamental.
    sound Tilting down yields warm, flute- or organ-like tones; tilting up produces bright, glassy textures.
OddEvenBalance   "Odd / Even" 0 1000 500 bip
    id odd_even_balance
    how Attenuates either even-numbered harmonics (left) or odd-numbered harmonics (right) above the fundamental.
    sound Odd only sounds hollow and woody, like a clarinet; even only sounds thin and octave-like; in the middle the full series sounds rich, like a saw.
PartialCount     "Partials" 0 63 31 int 1
    id partial_count
    how Sets the hard ceiling on how many harmonic sine waves are synthesized above the fundamental pitch.
    sound At 1 you hear a pure sine wave; increasing the count progressively builds harmonic complexity.
Inharmonicity    "Inharmonicity" 0 1000 0 pct
    id inharmonicity
    how Stretches upper partial frequencies away from integer multiples (partial n at n times the fundamental times the square root of 1 + B n squared).
    sound Transforms pure harmonic organ tones into stiff piano strings, chimes, and metallic bells.
HarmonicComb     "Spectral Comb" 0 1000 0 pct
    id harmonic_comb
    how Applies a sinusoidal amplitude notch mask across the 64 partials.
    sound Carves hollow, phaser-like vocal formants and resonant notches into the harmonic spectrum.
PartialShimmer   "Shimmer" 0 1000 0 pct
    id partial_shimmer
    how Introduces independent low-frequency amplitude and micro-pitch drift to upper partials.
    sound Creates a lush, living, choir-like movement across sustained chords.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 250 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 594 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 700 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 515 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 606 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnAdditiveMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
